{"id":"chatcmpl-cb7326cb-183b-40b2-8a29-e7ae6461b022","object":"chat.completion","created":1795229721,"model":"deepseek-v4.1-flash","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","reasoning_content":"","content":"```json\n{\n  \"highlights\": \"This task demonstrates how to resolve ambiguous anatomical findings in medical imaging by combining domain knowledge about standard anatomy with expert model consultation. The key insight is recognizing when a single view (lateral) lacks sufficient context and using specialized tools to interpret orientation-dependent findings. The pattern generalizes to any task where visual evidence must be disambiguated using domain-specific conventions.\",\n  \"patterns\": [\n    \"When visual evidence is ambiguous due to view orientation, consult a domain-specific expert model rather than relying on general reasoning alone.\",\n    \"Establish baseline anatomical conventions first (e.g., which structure is normally higher/anterior), then compare the observed image against that baseline to identify abnormality.\",\n    \"Recognize when a finding requires multi-view correlation (e.g., lateral vs frontal) and explicitly note the limitation before making a judgment.\",\n    \"Use tool calls strategically to offload specialized interpretation (e.g., expert QA models) when the reasoning path involves domain-specific conventions that general models may misapply.\"\n  ],\n  \"playbooks\": {\n    \"Medical Imaging Interpretation\": \"Always establish standard anatomical orientation conventions before judging abnormality; use expert models for view-specific ambiguities.\",\n    \"Visual Question Answering with Domain Conventions\": \"Identify whether the question depends on domain-specific conventions (laterality, orientation, normal baselines) and route to specialized tools when so.\",\n    \"Ambiguous Evidence Resolution\": \"When visual evidence supports multiple interpretations, explicitly state the baseline assumption and use a verification tool to confirm which interpretation holds.\"\n  },\n  \"checklists\": [\n    \"Confirm the imaging view (lateral vs frontal) and its implications for laterality and structure positioning before answering.\",\n    \"Verify the finding against standard anatomical baselines (which side is normally higher/anterior) and consult an expert tool if ambiguity remains.\"\n  ]\n}\n```"},"finish_reason":"stop","logprobs":null}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":1021,"total_tokens":1395,"completion_tokens":374,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0,"image_tokens":0,"text_tokens":1021},"completion_tokens_details":{"text_tokens":374}}}